# .claudeignore — retrieval-hygiene ignore list for Claude Code / agent tooling
#
# Purpose: keep generated, vendored, build and runtime trees OUT of retrieval and context
# loading, so an agent searching this repo sees source, tests and docs — not 3.7 GB of
# node_modules or 94 MB of duplicated translations.
#
# Syntax: gitignore-style (globs, `!` negation, trailing `/` = directory only).
# Consumers: Claude Code and other retrieval/indexing tools that honor Claude-style ignore
# files. `.cbmignore` covers the same intent for the codebase-memory MCP graph; `.gitignore`
# remains the canonical VCS list. A path is skipped only when a tool honors this file — it
# never affects git tracking or the Next.js build.
#
# Editing rules:
#   1. Never ignore source. `src/`, `open-sse/`, `bin/`, `tests/`, `scripts/`, `config/`,
#      `electron/` (source), `.github/`, `public/`, `skills/` and English `docs/**` must stay
#      searchable. Hiding them creates blind spots in code search and impact analysis.
#   2. Do not hide a path just because its name looks like data. Historical trap: `bin/` and
#      `src/lib/env/` were once ignored as "scratch/data" — they are real entrypoints and route
#      handlers. Verify with `git ls-files <path>` before adding a rule.
#   3. Generated-but-referenced assets can be ignored (translation mirrors, screenshots,
#      diagram exports) — regenerate them instead of reading them.
#   4. Prefer a narrow path over a broad pattern; a broad `.env*` must keep `!.env.example`.
#
# Audit after editing: `git ls-files | grep -vE '<this file's patterns>'` should still list
# every source directory, or use `node scripts/check/check-agent-rules.mjs` (asserts the
# ignore list never covers source roots).

# ── Dependencies / vendor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
vendor/
@omniroute/opencode-plugin/node_modules/
@omniroute/opencode-provider/node_modules/
obsidian-plugin/node_modules/

# ── Build output (reproducible) ────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
.next-playwright/
.build/
.out/
dist/
build/
out/
electron/dist-electron/
@omniroute/opencode-plugin/dist/
@omniroute/opencode-provider/dist/
src/mitm/tproxy/native/build/

# ── Generated artifacts, reports, caches ───────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.coverage/
reports/mutation/
.stryker-tmp/
stryker-output-*.json
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
quality-metrics.json
config/quality/quality-metrics.json
config/quality/test-impact-map.json
audit-report.json
scripts/i18n/_audit.json
scripts/i18n/_pending-keys.json
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.eslintcache-complexity
.eslintcache-probe
.cache/

# ── Runtime data, secrets, local state ─────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.homolog.example
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-journal
data/
.logs/
logs/*
.claude/scheduled_tasks/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/sessions/
.claude/state.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.agents/
.data/
.data-dev/
.local-data/
.artifacts/
.superpowers/
_staging/
tmp/

# ── Generated / mirrored documentation (large, regenerate instead) ─────────
# Translation mirrors duplicate the English docs tree; edit the English source.
docs/i18n/
# Exported diagram images are generated from `docs/diagrams/*.mmd` sources.
docs/diagrams/exported/
docs/screenshots/
docs/superpowers/

# ── Binary / media noise (not greppable) ───────────────────────────────────
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.ico
*.webp
*.pdf
*.zip
*.mp4
*.woff
*.woff2

# ── OS / editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.husky/_/

# ── DELIBERATELY KEPT VISIBLE (do not add rules for these) ─────────────────
# src/app/**, src/lib/**, src/domain/**, src/shared/**, src/server/**, src/mitm/** (TS source)
# open-sse/** (handlers, executors, translators, services, mcp-server source)
# bin/** (published CLI entrypoint), electron/** (main/preload source)
# tests/**, scripts/**, config/**, skills/**, public/**, examples/**, contrib/**
# .github/** (workflows, actions), package.json, tsconfig*.json, eslint.config.mjs
# docs/** in English (architecture, reference, security, frameworks, ops, routing, guides)
# AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md, README.md
# CHANGELOG.md is large: grep it narrowly, never open it whole (see AGENTS.md).
